  "2026-10-22T21:13:44.442Z",codex-agent,"Blocking numerical review follow-up: reproduce 100 independent units with bounds [1e16, 1e16 + 2], confidence 0.95, effect threshold 0, and identical 1e16 outcomes. Plan: normalize rewards before aggregation and confidence evaluation, preserve report reward units, and center the shared promotion margin before subtracting uncertainty. Cover tied and balanced outcomes across magnitudes and both directions, retain positive controls and effect-threshold semantics, record separate function-only revert proofs, and run unchanged complete npm/Bun release gates. Remote head pulled; main is already an ancestor. Prior seal-integrity work remains intact."
  "2026-10-22T21:21:47.932Z",codex-agent,"Numerical defect reproduced before the fix: the exact 100-unit [1e16, 1e16 + 2] tied case promotes with margin 0, and a balanced 50/50 endpoint cohort with opposite accumulation orders falsely reports a 2-point gain. Fix: evaluatePlan aggregates and applies confidence bounds on (reward - lower_bound) / reward_width, divides the effect threshold by the width, and restores only reported means to native units; statistical verdict fields explicitly use normalized units, documented in README and the report type. decidePromotion computes the mean difference before subtracting both confidence allowances and requires strictly positive observed improvement, also protecting legacy callers when uncertainty underflows or reward width is zero. Four targeted regressions pass 4/4; the property-style test covers 44 configurations (11 magnitudes/offsets, two directions, 10 or 100 independent units) with ties, balanced outcomes, powered positive controls and effect thresholds. Function-only revert proofs against b4ea1fa: reverting evaluatePlan plus decidePromotion fails the exact reproduction 0/1; reverting evaluatePlan alone fails the balanced-cohort test 0/1 with the shared gate fix retained; reverting decidePromotion alone fails its direct tie regression 0/1 with normalized evaluation retained. All functions restored afterward. npm ci succeeds with zero vulnerabilities; local typecheck, lint, duplicates, build and test compilation pass. Native and PM snapshot 47-test suites are running before complete release gates. Fresh complete GraphQL intake has no unresolved threads; latest nonempty CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings."
  "2026-10-22T21:26:51.793Z",codex-agent,"Final numerical self-review expanded the property test to 52 configurations, including both signs near Number.MAX_VALUE. A naive inverse normalization can reconstruct a finite endpoint as Infinity because the rounded reward width is added back to a large lower bound. evaluatePlan now reconstructs from the nearer endpoint. A fourth function-only revert restores the intermediate normalized evaluator with naive inverse conversion; the property regression fails 0/1 (Infinity versus Number.MAX_VALUE), while decidePromotion remains fixed. The three earlier function-only proofs were rerun against the final code and still fail 0/1 each. The initial native and PM snapshot suites passed 47/47, with evaluation-plan.ts at 100% lines/branches/functions and promotion.ts at 100% branches; final rebuilt targeted and snapshot runs include the expanded endpoint coverage. No threshold, scope, dependency pin or gate policy changed. Committed dist is absent; ignored dist is rebuilt. Full npm/Bun release counts will be recorded from the final candidate matrix."
