  "2026-10-22T21:43:10.882Z",codex-agent,"A fresh complete review refresh during numerical release verification found new thread PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6vYux4 (index.ts:5029): CLI plan show passes a short candidate id into strict canonical plan checks, producing a false drift refusal. Verified against the handler; register deliberately requires canonical plan-file identities, evaluate already resolves its Generation through getTypedItem, and generation registration already normalizes its reservation lookup. Fix the show command boundary with the configured project prefix, without requiring the not-yet-created candidate Generation. Add real-tracker command regressions for default and custom prefixes, compare short and canonical output before candidate creation, and record a handler-only revert proof. The next complete release matrix will cover the combined numerical and CLI fixes; no source change to numerical enforcement is needed. Latest CodeRabbit review contains this one finding and no outside-diff findings."
